{"seq":1,"slug":"cloud-security-foundations","title":"云安全基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cybersecurity-applied/cloud-native-security/cloud-security-foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"cloud-security-model","title":"云安全模型与责任","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cybersecurity-applied/cloud-native-security/cloud-security-foundations/cloud-security-model","wordCount":2188,"readingTime":9},{"seq":2,"slug":"cloud-native-threat-modeling","title":"云原生威胁模型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cybersecurity-applied/cloud-native-security/cloud-security-foundations/cloud-native-threat-modeling","wordCount":2164,"readingTime":9},{"seq":3,"slug":"zero-trust-architecture","title":"零信任架构","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cybersecurity-applied/cloud-native-security/cloud-security-foundations/zero-trust-architecture","wordCount":2648,"readingTime":11}],"introMarkdown":"# 云安全基础\n\n云安全基础是整个云原生安全知识体系的概念基石。本章不涉及具体工具配置或命令行操作，而是建立理解云原生安全所必需的三个核心框架：云服务的共享责任模型如何划分云厂商与客户之间的安全边界、云原生环境面临的独特威胁向量如何系统化地识别与建模、以及零信任架构如何从根本上重塑云环境的安全设计范式。\n\n理解这三个框架后，后续章节中的容器安全配置、Kubernetes 网络策略、密钥管理方案等具体技术才有了\"为什么这样做\"的理论依据。建议所有读者都先完成本章的学习，再进入后续的技术实践章节。\n"}